# Cursor BugBot Configuration for BSC Trading Bot

## Critical Bug Detection Priorities

### 1. Trading Logic Bugs (HIGHEST PRIORITY)
- Exit condition failures (TP/SL not triggering)
- Position monitoring failures
- Trade execution errors
- Price calculation errors
- Risk management bypasses

### 2. Runtime Errors
- Async/await unhandled promises
- Null/undefined reference errors
- Type mismatches in trade data
- Database connection failures
- RPC provider errors

### 3. Performance Issues
- Memory leaks in long-running processes
- Infinite loops in monitoring
- Rate limiter bypasses
- Database query inefficiencies
- Price history persistence failures

### 4. Security Vulnerabilities
- Private key exposure risks
- Unsigned transaction risks
- MEV exploitation vectors
- Rate limit bypasses
- Input validation failures

## Files to Monitor Closely
- agents/TradingStrategyAgent.js (position monitoring)
- AdvancedTradingBot.js (main bot logic)
- rangingStrategy.js (entry/exit logic)
- utils/priceHistoryManager.js (price data)
- security/rateLimiter.js (rate limiting)
- risk/productionRiskManager.js (risk checks)

## Known Issues to Watch
1. TP 0.8% never reached → Check exit condition logic
2. Max hold time not enforcing → Check cron job execution
3. position.side undefined → Check position creation logic
4. 0 exits in 11+ hours → Monitor executeExit() calls

## BugBot Alert Thresholds
- Any logger.error() calls
- Uncaught exceptions
- Process crashes
- Database write failures
- Transaction failures
